      "writtenOn": "2022-01-12T03:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Lukasz,\n\nYes you are right, Target_Latency may be a possible way to indicate to BAP Server during Config Codec operation to choose for Low Latency or High Reliability QoS Configuration settings, may not be a dependable though as it is left to BAP Server\u0027s implementations.\n\nHence, as you are also suggesting QoS Config may also be added if BAP Client wants to enforce QoS Configuration settings.\n\nAs you are already implementing to move the configuration to the json file, can you please incorporate this also ? Is there an ETA when the patch will be available ?\n\nWe are facing interoperability issues otherwise, raised a Buganizer request now related to this https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/214009192\n\nThanks and Regards,\nPartha Sarathi",
      "parentUuid": "1182d093_217d29e2",
      "revId": "073bdbb372ba723d754f5c2f5a4bb8bdaee88d93",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "664b85d7_96ffbfd6",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/le_audio_types.h",
